    <!-- =====================================================================
         PART L · PERFUMES
         ===================================================================== -->
    <h2 class="sec" id="part-l-perfumes-the-invisible-part-of-style">Part L · perfumes — the invisible part of style</h2>

    <div class="content-card">
      <div class="inline-card-title">Why perfume is fashion's most profitable product</div>
      <div class="lede-text-loose">Fragrance is the entry point to luxury. A bottle of Chanel No.5 costs a fraction of the dress it funds, yet carries the same brand DNA. The global fragrance market exceeds €50B per year. For major fashion houses, perfume and beauty can generate 30–50% of total revenue while requiring far less capital than garment production. Understanding fragrance — its families, longevity, and houses — is part of understanding fashion.</div>

