      {y:'1966',e:'Yves Saint Laurent creates "Le Smoking" — the women\'s tuxedo suit. The first time women wearing a man\'s suit was formal attire, not costume. Revolutionary.'},
      {y:'1960s',e:'Mod aesthetic dominates: geometric patterns, op-art prints, PVC boots. London\'s Carnaby Street becomes fashion capital temporarily displacing Paris.'},
      {y:'1970s',e:'Counter-culture aesthetics: hippie (flared jeans, peasant blouses), punk (ripped clothing, safety pins, subverted fashion grammar — Vivienne Westwood).'},
